# Web agents

Next.js 16 App Router, React 19, Chakra UI 3. Before a Next or Chakra API, read the installed docs (`node_modules/next/dist/docs/` or the Chakra MCP).

For multi-step web work, delegate to `.cursor/agents/` in this order. Skip a stage that does not apply and say why.

1. product-designer
2. ui-designer
3. explorer
4. api-implementer and ui-implementer, in parallel when they do not touch the same files
5. unit-tester
6. e2e-tester only when an e2e runner exists (this repo uses Jest)
7. code-reviewer
8. security-auditor when auth, uploads, secrets, forms, or HTML injection change
9. verifier

Send red type-check, lint, or test output to debugger. Invoke a specialist with `/name`.

Checks: `npm run type-check`, `npm run lint`, `npm test`. camelCase. No commits, pushes, or branch switches unless asked. Do not edit translation JSON. Leave the Next.js block in `AGENTS.md` unchanged.
